# Introduction

Johnston Engineering (JE) is pleased to submit this proposal for a Dual Trailer Vacuum Membrane Distillation (VMD) System to KMX Technologies.

This document provides a cost proposal for the design, analysis, procurement, fabrication and assembly tasks required for the Dual Trailer VMD System. Pricing milestones are divided into two phases: **Phase 1 ****–**** Full System Design and Analysis**, and **Phase 2 – ****Procurement****, ****Fabrication, and ****Assembly**. Johnston Engineering has conducted multiple SOW Review meetings with KMX and quoted KMX-provided hardware cost sheets and CAD files to drive the estimates in this proposal. 

The figures below are intended to convey a notional system layout. The images of the system below were originally provided by KMX. 

Figure 1 Notional system layout

Figure 2. Notional System Layout – Hardware quoted by Johnston Engineering is shown in **green**. Components shown in **gray** are either the responsibility of KMX or were not priced at the time of this proposal. Hardware highlighted in **yellow** represents placeholder estimates based on comparable components.

Several potential cost-driving items have not yet been quoted by Johnston Engineering but have been estimated by KMX. These include:
• Vacuum pumps
• Blowers
• Membranes

