# Project Timeline

The complete project duration is 210 labor days, assuming four staff per labor category. If the project kicks off in January 2026, **Phase****s 1**** ****&**** ****2**** can be completed ****by ****end of Q2**** 2026.**** **

Johnston Engineering has the capacity to increase staffing if an accelerated schedule is desired. While adding personnel can shorten the overall timeline, increasing team size means more engineers must review and digest the same information, resulting in natural duplication of some effort. For this reason, an expedited timeline may increase labor costs by approximately 5%.

# Pricing and Billing Process

This proposal is based on a time and material (T&M) hourly rate of $205 for time and a 25% markup for materials. Labor is billed at a rate of $205 per hour, hardware purchased, and subcontractors are billed on a cost-plus structure of cost +25%. 95% of material and equipment expenses have been estimated at this stage of the proposal. Johnston Engineering has provided a detailed costing of materials under Exhibit A of this proposal.

Johnston Engineering works from a retainer payment agreement. All services are pre-paid in monthly reserved hours. Unused hours do not expire and will roll over to the following month. At every invoice cycle, Johnston Engineering provides the Client with its current positive or negative balance and makes recommendations for future hourly purchases. All invoices are due on receipt. Upon project completion, any remaining hours can be used for future KMX projects or refunded at the sole discretion of KMX.

Our billing process is broken down into detailed categories allowing KMX to see exactly how much time was spent on each task. For each labor charge, invoices will detail the date, labor category, description of work performed, and hours used. For materials charges, invoices will detail the date, description of the hardware, and cost.

# Intellectual Property Rights

Johnston Engineering will assign all intellectual property related to this project to KMX Technologies. Johnston Engineering is willing to assist KMX and patent attorneys with IP-related communications such as in transferring IP, generating patent figures, etc. We have not budgeted any IP transfer time in this proposal.

